s not just his role. So in this case my role would be that I provide for the family, I go outside and work; I don't have the ability to stay home and do my wife's role of cooking or cleaning or whatever. This is the distinction. When you use the word role, it doesn't change the fact that you didn't only say it's just [roles], something that they're doing, but you said they also don't have the ability to exercise the other's roles.", "So now your analogy falls apart, because you were trying to say that's only the role of the son and the father cannot do it. If the father can do the same thing that the son can do, then your analogy doesn't work anymore, because the verse here is saying only one can do something.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Passionate Christian Argues For The Trinity With A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ntsF1iRj8IM", ((2548, "42:28–43:11"), (2605, "43:25–43:53"), (2680, "44:40–45:16"), (2793, "46:33–47:46"), (2890, "48:10–48:30"),), id: 3851)
