#passage(("That's not how every Christian has interpreted the verse, because you have many groups of Christianity that disagree with you. The earlier groups of Christianity, like the Ebionites and the Nazarenes, did not believe Jesus was God. They believed he's just a Messenger of God. You have today Unitarian Christians. You have Jehovah's Witnesses, which you don't consider Christians, but they don't believe Jesus is divine. There are many other Christians that would interpret the verses different from what you're interpreting them.", "But what you just admitted to is that there is no clear verses saying any of your beliefs. So if it's an inference, that's what inference by definition means: you don't have a clear explicit statement stating what you're saying. So you have to infer the meaning, which can be right and can be wrong. As a Muslim, I'm not going to base my Afterlife on an inference of maybe, maybe yes. Some Christians believe this, some Christians believe that. On the other hand, I did not bring you inferences. I brought you a clear cut verse in John:14: \"The Father is greater than I\". Clear, no inference, I don't need to add anything from myself.", "It's about the Truth. And the Truth is always clear. Now, the God in the Bible says \"God is not the author of confusion\" (1Corinthians14:33). The Bible says that \"come, let us reason together\" (Isaiah1:18). \"Let us reason\": that's how we come to the conclusion of the Truth. Now, you've given me all of these ambiguous verses that are not clear, that I've already given you responses for. Now, I gave you one clear verse.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Christian Attempts To Convert Muslim Then Instantly Regrets It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ppqugzwmKcg", ((1556, "25:56–26:15"), (1579, "26:19–26:56"), (1680, "28:00–28:26"),), id: 3865)
