#passage(("This person says, \"The Quran proves Jesus is God.\" She says the word of Allah. The verse is refuting her and her own religion, completely, in every way. But she took a part of the verse and misread it intentionally, and then made that argument. So let's read what the verse actually says.", "The verse says (anNisa4:171), (Oh People of the Scripture) يَـٰٓأَهْلَ ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ لَا تَغْلُوا۟ فِى دِينِكُمْ (Do not go into extremes in your religion). Do not exaggerate in your religion. وَلَا تَقُولُوا۟ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلْحَقَّ (Do not say anything about Allah except the Ttruth). Then what does Allahﷻ ('Azza wa Jal: Almighty and Majestic is He) say? إِنَّمَا ٱلْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ٱبْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولُ ٱللَّهِ. First thing is (Jesus the Messiah is the Messenger from God). So Allah is saying: do not go into extreme, do not exaggerate in your religion, do not pretend that Jesus was more than this. He was the Messenger from God. So the Quran first described him as a Messenger.", "Then Allah says وَكَلِمَتُهُۥٓ, and the Word of Allah, أَلْقَىٰهَآ إِلَىٰ مَرْيَمَ. So Allah has given His Word to Marry, or sent His Word to Marry. What is that talking about? It's not saying, \"and Jesus is the Word of Allah\". The verse doesn't say that. It says the Word of Allah, Allah gave to Marry. What is that Word? Allah describes that in the Quran (alimran3:59). Allah says (the example of Jesus unto Allah is like of Adam.) Allah said to him (\"Be\" and it is) كُن فَيَكُونُ. This is \"the Word\", as all Muslims believe and as the Quran itself explains: this is \"The Word of the Creation\", \"BE, and it is\". This is the Word that Allah has given to Marry. This is the Word that was told to Marry: without any male intervention, Allah said to Jesus, \"Be\", and it is. So Allah created him. So this verse of the Quran is saying \"Jesus is a Messenger of God\", number one. Number two is saying that Jesus is created by the Word of God, \"Be and it is\".", "And then a Spirit from Allah preceded: وَرُوحٌۭ مِّنْهُ (And a spirit from Allah). Why is that a spirit? Allah sent the angel Gabriel. And angel Gabriel is called الروح (arRuh: the spirit). This is one of the titles of angel Gabriel. And he's the one who came to Marry. Allah says in the Quran (alQadr97:4), تَنَزَّلُ ٱلْمَلَـٰٓئِكَةُ وَٱلرُّوحُ (The angels descend and arRuh): arRuh is Gabriel. So this verse is saying that Jesus is created through angel Gabriel and the Word of Allah, \"BE\", and it is. And he's a Messenger from God.", "Is that it? No! Then Allahﷻ says فَـَٔامِنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦ (Then believe in Allah and His Messengers), like Jesus. وَلَا تَقُولُوا۟ ثَلَـٰثَةٌ (Do not say three). DO NOT SAY THREE! So the verse is refuting the Trinity! So the verse is not only refuting what you're claiming, which is the divinity of Jesus. It's also refuting your whole Trinity. And then it says إِنَّمَا ٱللَّهُ إِلَـٰهٌۭ وَٰحِدٌۭ (Allah is one God). سُبْحَـٰنَهُۥٓ أَن يَكُونَ لَهُۥ وَلَدٌۭ ۘ (Glorified is He that he would have a child). So it refutes the idea of Allah having a son. It refutes the Trinity. And it refutes that Jesus is anything more than a Messenger of God. And Allah says: do not exaggerate in your religion; Allah, God, is ONLY ONE.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((2, "0:02–1:13"), (73, "1:13–1:50"), (111, "1:51–2:45"), (171, "2:51–3:30"), (211, "3:31–4:11"),), id: 4252)
