ot responsible because some maniacs believe incorrect things against what the prophet believes, or people create new religions. Nobody's going to come and say it's better Prophet Muhammad didn't come. It doesn't matter, even if hundreds of years after someone comes and brings a new belief and changes the scripture. It doesn't matter, because there's other people who follow, because people have believed the message of the prophet, and the people followed him, and the prophet has delivered his message. It's not upon him to keep people in line and check for the rest of eternity. It's his job to give people the message. And then it's upon them to believe or not. So the message of Jesus was a complete perfect success, as it is the message of all prophets and messengers. They give the message, and that is the role.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Becomes Speechless After Being Presented With The Christian Dilemma! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z_W9m77uuyE", ((2465, "41:05–41:54"), (2538, "42:18–42:59"), (2580, "43:00–43:35"), (2615, "43:35–44:08"), (2756, "45:56–46:32"), (2792, "46:32–47:23"),), id: 4277)

