#passage(("The only source for the death of Jesus on the cross is the Bible. And the Bible is not by eyewitness accounts. Whatever you have today, the earliest manuscript you have is written 400 years separate from Jesus. It's called the Sinaiticus; it's the earliest full Bible that you have. You have nothing from the first century. Barely anything from the first century. Late second century, there is a card, P52, and it doesn't have any relevant information to do with the cross or divinity or anything like that. So when it comes to the death and resurrection, there isn't any eyewitness accounts for the person who says Jesus was crucified that they can present us as evidence that it happened.", "Now, historians generally will record that Jesus was crucified. Why? Because historians generally record that human beings died. You don't record miracles. Any historian: OK, it was a human. A human was killed. Makes sense, of course. We, on the other hand, believe that he was raised up. Even the Christians believe in the Ascension after. But this is a miracle that historians are not going to record. They don't believe in it. They would just record the human being died and that was it, because that's what historians generally record.", "Not only that, Allah tells us in the Quran that it was made to appear to the people as if Jesus was crucified (anNisa4:157). What is the wisdom behind that? The clear wisdom behind that is that they're not going to look for him anymore. They're not going to chase him anymore trying to kill him. And then after that, the ascension happened and Allah took him up.", "So we don't believe in the crucifixion. We would rely on the Quran as a source, over anything else, to tell us accurate history, and that can never change! Rather than relying on something that has already changed -referring to the Bible- or does not have any originals, or accurate manuscripts. That would be our position.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Gets Questioned On The Treatm