#passage(("Chapter:4, Verse:157: the original or the Arabic text does not say \"but another was made to resemble him\". \"Another\" is in brackets, so that's not in the Quran. The Quran doesn't say that. That is just an opinion of someone, or an opinion that some people held, but that's not what the Quran is saying, and that's not what the Prophet said.", "If we were to translate it word for word, Allah says: (An-Nisaa4: 157) وَقَوْلِهِمْ (And their statement) إِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيحِ (We killed the Messiah) عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ (Jesus, the son of Mary) وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوهُ (They did not kill him, nor did they crucify him.) وَلَكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ (It was made to appear onto them so.) وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ لَفِي شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ ۚ (Those who differ about him are in doubt), meaning people don't know exactly what happened. And then Allah says: وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ يَقِينًا (And surely they did not kill him). And then Allah says in the next verse: بَل رَّفَعَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ (Allah raised Jesus to Himself), meaning up to the heaven. And he was not killed nor crucified. That is literally what the Quran says. So this idea of someone being put in his place is not from the Quran or the Prophet. And if you read other translations, you'll see that they don't say that part, because it's in brackets.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “40 Year Evangelist Challenges Muslim On The Crucifixion Of Jesus! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RIPUEGsRKSs", ((65, "1:05–1:36"), (99, "1:39–2:31"),), id: 4310)
