#passage(("It does not matter whether they believed he did or he didn't, because that does not change whether they go to paradise or not. If I was a Muslim and I lived at the time of Jesus, and I believed that he died, that he was killed, or crucified, that is not going to affect whether I go to paradise or not. What matters is his teachings. The reason it's a problem for you Christians –and I don't mean that offensively– the reason you guys find it a problem is because you already have a package that you put on the crucifixion. That package is the original sin, that actually his death was not a normal death but the death that took all the sins of the world. You're putting all of that package on that specific verse, but that package is not there. So, there's no deception there, because whether people believed he was killed or he was not killed, if they unintentionally or wrongfully believed that he was actually killed, as Muslims, and they follow these teachings, then there's no problem; they go to paradise.", "You are asking me about something that happened in the past, from The Unseen, meaning I have not observed them with my own eyes. So, if Allah does not tell me the exact details, or the Hadith does not tell me the exact details, and I was not there, you can not expect me to give you the exact details of what happened, but we have the conclusion. I was not there 2000 years ago. But there's a difference there. When you ask about a historical event, it is not the same as when you ask about the Quran, because we have manuscripts of it. It's a written text that we have carbon-dated manuscripts from the first century. That is not equal to an event that happened that you're expecting me to tell you the details of it. There's no comparison. It's a false equivalent.", "So, what the Quran gives you is the conclusion. The conclusion is that people believed he was killed or crucified. But Allah saved him. And perhaps there's a wisdom behind them believing that he's killed or crucified, so they don't look for him anymore. And his people, his disciples, if they followed his teachings, just to worship one God Alone, not to worship Him, and there's no Trinity, then they go to paradise from an Islamic point of view. There's Zero deception there. There's no problem actually from an Islamic point of view. There is only a problem from Christian point of view.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Family Grills Muslim On His Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKqmYTyocyo", ((1203, "20:03–20:53"), (1269, "21:09–21:59"), (1319, "21:59–22:40"),), id: 4311)
