ucified. So, it affirms what the Quran is saying, that the people don't know what they're talking about. And he is pushing it like some sort of a historical fact. We're going to ask him: bring us one eyewitness to the crucifixion.", "They would quote Eusebius, [Tacitus]. They were just historians writing history. They were not eyewitnesses to the crucifixions themselves. So, again, they don't support you. They're just writing what people said, the hearsay. And we said we don't have an issue with that. In fact, that is in line with the narrative of the Quran. If it appeared to the people so, then people will be saying that he was crucified. But, the reality is that he wasn't. And you can see a wisdom in that. If people believe that he was crucified, they're not going to look out for him after. He will be safe. So, we don't have an issue with saying that some people believed in historically, but where is your proof? Have no eyewitnesses for it. So, how is it one of the most believable historical facts? You don't have any proof for it that you can present for us.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Wess Huff Claims The Quran Was Copied From The Bible | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hb-kHiXbGxI", ((1829, "30:29–30:53"), (1855, "30:55–31:25"), (1887, "31:27–32:10"), (1935, "32:15–32:37"), (1968, "32:48–33:38"),), id: 4331)
