ming that someone is telling us that. But whoever told us they ran away, he never told us they came back. Which verse mentions that they specifically came and witnessed the Crucifixion? Who's writing this? Nobody knows!", "You got forgeries, because you have a person who's allegedly a Jewish (Flavius Josephus quoted by Eusebius) who's writing about Jesus resurrecting and this and that, but he is not accepting Christianity, which obviously makes no sense. I can accept the account that they're not forgeries, but the historians were writing the word of people. People said he was crucified, so people recorded that he was crucified. But that's not an eyewitness account. None of them say that we witnessed this; they're just writing history! No Christian can prove that Jesus was crucified. Not a single Christian.", "Now historians agree, consensus, that Jesus died. But we say: because historians record history, they don't record miracles! Historians say Jesus was a human being, and all human beings die! So obviously, they're all going to agree that Jesus died, because they all believe that human beings die. So we don't have an issue with them recording that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Researcher Demands Evidence Against The Crucifixion Of Jesus! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IVUeaRBg02o", ((2154, "35:54–36:48"), (2215, "36:55–37:33"), (2272, "37:52–38:48"), (2337, "38:57–40:00"), (2403, "40:03–40:53"), (2489, "41:29–42:12"), (2548, "42:28–43:31"), (2618, "43:38–43:55"),), id: 4332)
