 Saturday, the day of Sunday and the night of Sunday, and that was not the case! Like we said, Friday evening and Saturday before dawn when it was dark or at dawn time! How's this 3 days and 3 nights? And some Christians try to play a game and say: Oh! day actually means a period of time in Hebrew or whatever. It says \"day and night\", so it can only refer to the 24 hours that we refer to, so this game doesn't work. So you see a problem in the account of the crucifixion.", "On top of all of that, I'm going to add the last thing, because I can go on and on using the Bible and show you through the Bible that your account of the crucifixion is a bunch of nonsense. In (Matthew4:6), (Psalms91:9-12) is quoted about Jesus: how God is going to protect Jesus with the angels and stuff. It's quoting this prophecy, or this Psalm let's say, about Jesus in the Old Testament. Now, when we read the Psalm, what does it say? The (Psalm91:15) says, (if he calls upon God, God will truly answer him). Did Jesus call upon God to save him from crucifixion? Yes, he did! He said: \"Take this cup away from me\" (Mark14:36). So he called upon God to save him from the crucifixion! Muslims believe that God saved him from that, he wasn't crucified or killed! So exactly according to that account, it says that God will send angels to protect him. He will not be bruised, he will not be harmed. All the chapter is about protection, and how God will send angels and answer his prayers and all of that. We believe that he was raised up (anNisa4:158). So these angels came and they raised Jesus up. This Islamic narrative is affirmed and confirmed with your own Bible.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Disproving Islam In 2 Minutes?! The Quran Teaches People To Lie?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nLUKAN1votI", ((1000, "16:40–17:14"), (1037, "17:17–17:45"), (1069, "17:49–19:01"), (1143, "19:03–20:02"),), id: 4337)
