#passage(("In Islam (alA'raf7:20), we have Satan enticing Adam and Eve, both of them, to disobey God and eat from the tree, when Allah commanded Adam and Eve not to eat from the tree. And it doesn't mention what type of tree it is; it just mentions the tree, because the type of tree doesn't really matter. And then they disobeyed God, and then Allah teaches them how to repent. So the point of this incident is for Allah to teach humanity - the progeny of Adam - what to do when they commit sins. If you commit such a grave sin, what do you do? You repent to God. How do you repent? Allah taught Adam how to repent. So Allah says in the Quran (alBaqara2:36-37) فَتَلَقَّى آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ فَتابَ عَلَيْهِ: Adam received Words from his Lord; how to repent, teaching him (alBaqara2:37). So Allah repented upon Adam.", "But Allah in the Quran describes it as a \"slip\" (alBaqara2:36) فَأَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطَانُ (They slipped). Satan pulled their legs, they slipped, they made a mistake and they repented to God, and God forgave them. The story in Islam is about a lesson for humanity, for what to do when you sin, and that lesson was taught to Adam before Adam was sent to earth: this is what you do when you will disobey God, when you will sin, and God will command you to do something; this is how you act. Both Adam and Eve did the problem, both of Adam and Eve were held accountable, and both of them were forgiven by God. This is the Islamic perspective.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Debates Muslim On The Original Sin! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BjYGPQ-G5RM", ((62, "1:02–1:48"), (112, "1:52–2:29"),), id: 4376)
